# Paths whose change gets a security review before the merge request (#742).
#
# One bash pattern per line, matched against each changed path in full; `*`
# matches across `/`, so `internal/egress/*` covers the whole tree. Blank
# lines and `#` comments are ignored. The `pr-guards` workflow labels a PR
# that matches any line `needs-security-review`. A PR that makes the hub
# trust something a loop controls without touching these is labelled by
# hand (CONVENTIONS.md).

# Where a loop, a person or the network reaches the hub.
# cmd/spool binds the listeners, checks --trusted-host, prints the operator
# token and admin password on first start, and runs `spool user` and
# `spool token`.
cmd/spool/*
internal/httpapi/*
internal/route/*
internal/surface/*
internal/users/*
internal/operator/*

# The wall between a loop and the rest: its workstation, its way out, its hook.
internal/runtime/*
internal/egress/*
internal/hook/*
internal/attach/*
internal/loop/actor.go
cmd/spool-egress/*
cmd/spool-hook/*
docker/*

# Where a credential rests, and what keeps one out of the record.
internal/store/*
internal/datadir/*
internal/redact/*
scripts/secret-*
scripts/spool-backup*
scripts/spool-restore*
scripts/security-paths*

# What runs with the repo's token, and what the shipped code pulls in.
.github/workflows/*
# Scripts a workflow runs with a write token (secret-* is listed above).
scripts/advisories.sh
scripts/community-welcome.sh
.github/security-review-paths
go.mod
go.sum
web/package.json
web/package-lock.json
